From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mikael Hug <mikaelhug@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 23:07:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] nvme-apple: Disable the deferred flush work in remove

apple_nvme_delayed_flush() checks that the controller is live and then
queues flush_dwork. A flush that passed the check just before remove()
moved the controller to DELETING can queue the work after remove() has
flushed it, and the work then runs on a namespace that
nvme_remove_namespaces() has freed.

Disable the work after flushing it. A deferred flush cancelled this way
was already completed to the block layer, and the controller shutdown
that follows writes back the volatile cache.

Fixes: dca0a3c3edb9 ("nvme-apple: run the deferred flush before remove and suspend")
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
(cherry picked from commit 9c791fdb3f4ecf274f9c68dd028bd5893ce45613)
---
 drivers/nvme/host/apple.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/nvme/host/apple.c b/drivers/nvme/host/apple.c
index 2a76249..a8544f3 100644
--- a/drivers/nvme/host/apple.c
+++ b/drivers/nvme/host/apple.c
@@ -1706,6 +1706,7 @@ static void apple_nvme_remove(struct platform_device *pdev)
 
 	nvme_change_ctrl_state(&anv->ctrl, NVME_CTRL_DELETING);
 	flush_delayed_work(&anv->flush_dwork);
+	disable_delayed_work_sync(&anv->flush_dwork);
 	flush_work(&anv->ctrl.reset_work);
 	nvme_stop_ctrl(&anv->ctrl);
 	nvme_remove_namespaces(&anv->ctrl);
